# Files vendored from outside this project keep the bytes their authors
# published, on every platform.
#
# `tests/samples/external/` holds samples fetched byte-for-byte from pinned
# commits, and `SOURCES.md` records that claim - `tests/test_bai2_external.py`
# pins one of them by SHA-256. Without this, a Windows checkout with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every LF to CRLF, so the file on disk is not the
# file the commit holds: the BAI2 sample hashes to 0258766c... instead of
# 0150331e..., and that test failed on windows-latest and nowhere else (#57).
#
# The NACHA samples were being rewritten the same way and nothing caught it,
# because `nacha.inspect` strips a line before reading it. They passed while
# reading a file moov never published, which is the opposite of what an outside
# sample is for.
#
# `-text`, not `binary`: no end-of-line conversion either way, and diffs stay
# readable.
tests/samples/external/** -text
